      "text": "What if I told you that you could stand in four different US states without taking a single step? Sounds impossible, right? But there's actually a place where you can do exactly that. It's called the Four Corners Monument, located in the American Southwest. Look at this map. Arizona, Utah, Colorado, and New Mexico all meet at one single point. And here's what's incredible. It's the only place in the entire United States where four state borders come together. There's even a marker on the ground showing the exact spot where all four states meet. So, if you ever visit, which state would you stand in first?",
      "start_time": 0.22,
      "end_time": 36.1,
      "speaker": {
        "id": "speaker_0",
